[{:db/id "q-129100/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5a6e7e2e-8e2d-56fa-9404-e7e906b75117" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129100/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "7e8a1f4b-0370-5f4f-9f89-4c4efeaff742" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129100/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "01d9145c-b484-579b-918d-29cc61be229c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129100/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "930bf38c-95a5-5e07-b7a1-cab2e79b5552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129100/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "c0809196-b366-5886-afff-771bfdd37057" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129100/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5158d59b-b675-5738-8559-519928423666" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129100/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-129100/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-129100/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-129100/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-129100/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-129100/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129100" :question/id #uuid "9353c0c9-bae4-5a82-8f86-8a66dcc33c88" :question/math-academy-id "q-129100" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(8,-3,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨7,-2,4⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(7,-2,4).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨7,-2,4⟩-⟨8,-3,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2-3-6|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129100/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129100"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129096/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" :answer/id #uuid "3b9cc1a3-4182-5d11-8c32-a7b1c8321524" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129096/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5ea0781d-1f2c-5483-ac1b-5c0bfa0d37b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129096/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "acddab0d-878a-5586-bc68-cd002d591acc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129096/selection/471d022dc8477dee5b5835181abb5643fcc83818c373aaad08fa968767db722e" :answer/id #uuid "f4cda5a8-1f20-5dcf-bc69-1ae1c841827c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129096/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0b517386-0a37-550a-afa6-10a941a7f19e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129096/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eab66f8f-3b6c-5f1d-a169-55650145efe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129096/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-129096/selection/53a62adc469f7106cfcc253972af70d0b351ee4c505c92859749c553ee85bd38" "q-129096/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-129096/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-129096/selection/471d022dc8477dee5b5835181abb5643fcc83818c373aaad08fa968767db722e" "q-129096/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129096" :question/id #uuid "9bb1faa8-11a4-5693-ba1f-eb7ce0c1d034" :question/math-academy-id "q-129096" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-3,1,4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨3,-2,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨-2,4,-4⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(3,-2,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-2,1⟩-⟨-3,1,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,-3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,-4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|6\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129096/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129096"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33466"] :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3,5,-2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(5,9,0).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 2+2\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+8-8|}{\\sqrt{4+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4|}{\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34031"] :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,2,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨1,-5,3⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,0,4⟩=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(1,-5,3).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-5,3⟩-⟨-1,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-7,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨1,0,4⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot 1+(-7)\\cdot 0+6\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+0+24|}{\\sqrt{1+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26|}{\\sqrt{17}} \\\\  & =\\frac{26\\sqrt{17}}{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-129095/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0943c76d-8269-50d0-8ebb-f16db809f19e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129095/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" :answer/id #uuid "8a1852da-a82d-5bba-a826-62663fc36b87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129095/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "2d3745e4-0077-5cc1-95c4-23f183e8d15c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129095/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" :answer/id #uuid "7d92171f-985a-5194-a50c-92c052f7a1d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129095/selection/34219f229a95b374101226ed6e8380124ab0bbcf04f479caa9d1b203ca15969e" :answer/id #uuid "1c5f0d86-eb33-5e94-9961-804a6ca6e29b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129095/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2f0cd1b7-d3da-5d3a-8181-93b5a30c1b28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129095/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" :answer-field/choices ["q-129095/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-129095/selection/80f9bea33aa6a89d127ee9002c35787893c3c59b57df469ba089cea1a4a6a472" "q-129095/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-129095/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" "q-129095/selection/34219f229a95b374101226ed6e8380124ab0bbcf04f479caa9d1b203ca15969e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129095" :question/id #uuid "f5c4a0dd-1327-5c31-a6f8-74a677ca7ac3" :question/math-academy-id "q-129095" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(2,-1,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-3)\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12-6-4|}{\\sqrt{16+4+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-22|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129095/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f53201a-0d75-5f17-b869-009c8e0523c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129095"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-34074/selection/f5740f9b052e6ba49d250c5330beb8234317361db13f138aa5c402482269e3a5" :answer/id #uuid "e9086f44-9d13-5c7e-bb71-2f4b1d8dca58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11\\sqrt{26}}{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34074/selection/37e3175a7f6e90a1fe6bb2dadbc41a038984d778f5e4a02e84a4f8e21f5b6896" :answer/id #uuid "aa782961-f528-5cc0-99db-7cb04f4afdd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{43}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34074/selection/ef5efb9e8e598d36156955f4780f88030ac76a77c6431c3eba64524c3ce49d04" :answer/id #uuid "5e978026-1334-50a4-90c1-fd1e096367c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{48}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34074/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "c0bbf0d5-2b7a-525c-9cf8-8a212156c96f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34074/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4e9d4ed6-9643-578c-a211-11a717c851c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-34074/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f04bd9c4-12e4-5ade-9a50-bd0e70fe054f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-34074/selection/37e3175a7f6e90a1fe6bb2dadbc41a038984d778f5e4a02e84a4f8e21f5b6896" :answer-field/choices ["q-34074/selection/f5740f9b052e6ba49d250c5330beb8234317361db13f138aa5c402482269e3a5" "q-34074/selection/37e3175a7f6e90a1fe6bb2dadbc41a038984d778f5e4a02e84a4f8e21f5b6896" "q-34074/selection/ef5efb9e8e598d36156955f4780f88030ac76a77c6431c3eba64524c3ce49d04" "q-34074/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-34074/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-34074" :question/id #uuid "f3a72fe2-3dee-598e-8f40-0b69c3921f39" :question/math-academy-id "q-34074" :question/problem "Given that $Q(2,4,1)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,2,9⟩=5$, find the shortest distance from $P(6,-1,0)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,4,1⟩-⟨6,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-6,2,9⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-6)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 9|}{\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{9}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|24+10+9|}{\\sqrt{36+4+81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|43|}{\\sqrt{121}} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-34074/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-34074"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129102/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6a021570-d057-5990-90d1-4b089d124d7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129102/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "4121a510-a275-5426-b359-62b90f0b4d8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129102/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "9645d86b-25a3-5085-af30-176a9544c3c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129102/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c0ba8bcc-dd78-543e-905f-28c62d67ea3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129102/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "efa9c94b-076e-5b1e-867a-0dd554335634" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129102/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf17f808-2d80-5762-96cb-c48a69767c4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129102/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-129102/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-129102/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-129102/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-129102/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-129102/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129102" :question/id #uuid "8940db6b-36ca-5af7-90d3-112c28f5c42c" :question/math-academy-id "q-129102" :question/problem "Given that $Q(4,-2,8)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,6,2⟩=-8$, find the shortest distance from $P(3,-4,2)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-2,8⟩-⟨3,-4,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,2,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-3,6,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 6+6\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-3+12+12|}{\\sqrt{9+36+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|21|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129102/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129102"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80049/selection/974f1e09406a3c6be062f79ae2c99a3f9162780580a069e1cc5bf211a15adf21" :answer/id #uuid "1fe74019-90c7-56ae-a6db-b9792c8659db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80049/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" :answer/id #uuid "d5dbb4f7-a168-5c56-ba5f-427586a8ca88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80049/selection/3ef1e9fe0989826760fa6d9bec1c8ea06d4454b7755de12f7ecf198c6fc61afb" :answer/id #uuid "d860b881-ac6e-5c4f-8deb-ef47d7352a54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13\\sqrt{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80049/selection/181d1f839d214e5807f4235aba03fc371467f433c702fbf48b29ccfdaa41b68d" :answer/id #uuid "aef8c0f8-5bff-53ed-94eb-9f3509d2c564" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80049/selection/982c9c3802fed6a4a5ab68bd633ca7ec0d0709423d870f44136a8183fe97766c" :answer/id #uuid "0ad6d0cf-316c-53f5-83dd-40500e598bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80049/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b28316c9-bd52-50a8-9c35-e588b75348a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80049/selection/982c9c3802fed6a4a5ab68bd633ca7ec0d0709423d870f44136a8183fe97766c" :answer-field/choices ["q-80049/selection/974f1e09406a3c6be062f79ae2c99a3f9162780580a069e1cc5bf211a15adf21" "q-80049/selection/0c8b08d4b198d89c5fe756f861bd5b37e398d2a5b3237908210d9646370a666f" "q-80049/selection/3ef1e9fe0989826760fa6d9bec1c8ea06d4454b7755de12f7ecf198c6fc61afb" "q-80049/selection/181d1f839d214e5807f4235aba03fc371467f433c702fbf48b29ccfdaa41b68d" "q-80049/selection/982c9c3802fed6a4a5ab68bd633ca7ec0d0709423d870f44136a8183fe97766c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80049" :question/id #uuid "a8c5c6cc-9743-5139-a5ed-91098db233ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-80049" :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,3,4)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-4,2,0⟩=2$, find the shortest distance from $P(5,-2,3)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,3,4⟩-⟨5,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-4,2,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot (-4)+5\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 0|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|16+10+0|}{\\sqrt{16+4+0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26|}{\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80049/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80049"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-34075"] :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,3,5)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-4,1,-3⟩=-16$, find the shortest distance from $P(-3,7,3)$ to $Π.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,3,5⟩-⟨-3,7,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-4,1,-3⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4\\cdot (-4)+(-4)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-3)|}{\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-16-4-6|}{\\sqrt{16+1+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-26|}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-129148/selection/251241e3e29e66ae574bf93834cfbf6d510639c43261d8b9f81dd9c88b9b888a" :answer/id #uuid "4f537269-a779-5285-a570-72fce626ef0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{10}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129148/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "76f0a136-ef05-5ea4-a933-6e45a01c6050" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129148/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3e61f1ff-7ba8-59ff-b1aa-d5539d7f955d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129148/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "ddb98251-7e11-5ea0-9523-5fa63e1bdb3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129148/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "1f06b796-520e-5af2-8fd9-060978d672e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129148/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5f60066-2f65-5f20-89ac-f79523e0a547" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129148/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-129148/selection/251241e3e29e66ae574bf93834cfbf6d510639c43261d8b9f81dd9c88b9b888a" "q-129148/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-129148/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-129148/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-129148/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129148" :question/id #uuid "d807d18c-0ed9-5a1c-93ec-7370ba4c718f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129148" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,3,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩=16.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,6⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2x-3y+6z & =16 \\\\ 2x & =6z-3y-16 \\\\ x & =3z-\\frac{3}{2}y-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $y=2$ and $z=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nx=3-\\frac{3}{2}(2)-8=-8.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(-8,2,1)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-8,2,1⟩-⟨5,3,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-13,-1,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-2,-3,6⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-13)\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+(-6)\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|26+3-36|}{\\sqrt{4+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129148/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a50c5f1-fbda-5c87-afa2-32495c69c18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129148"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129166/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "72d402c0-8438-58ba-af7d-f47a5d124e62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129166/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "51b28277-6857-5e25-9bce-761ad44a0247" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129166/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "03d47dcb-fcb4-5bd1-8428-6a87574f87f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129166/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "825deea4-4cf1-5e5b-a05c-5b46c7ac80a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129166/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "536e7f66-48bd-57eb-b77c-765655b4ffc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129166/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a94c1631-4c52-5d65-abe7-022a6cb49ace" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129166/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-129166/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-129166/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-129166/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-129166/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-129166/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129166" :question/id #uuid "c70bb623-12db-507f-b2a7-384f90211edf" :question/math-academy-id "q-129166" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,3,-6)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-x+2y+2z=8.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-2$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+2y+2z & =8 \\\\ -1(-2)+2(1)+2z & =8 \\\\ 2z & =4 \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-2,1,2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-2,1,2⟩-⟨-2,3,-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-1,2,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|0\\cdot (-1)+(-2)\\cdot 2+8\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|0-4+16|}{\\sqrt{1+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129166/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129166"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129160/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" :answer/id #uuid "7e1954fb-f2bb-57a9-a28d-e71eb639a2fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129160/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "e278d387-a6e8-5749-ba01-0b24ec322330" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129160/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "b950195d-e13b-55c3-980d-1e121a1b70ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129160/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "dd7403b5-598d-5071-904e-c2bf87240bf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129160/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d5efca43-4725-5dbe-bfb1-31c9c6ba5751" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129160/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c69f7c31-30be-5732-b00b-a4480dd7fdfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129160/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer-field/choices ["q-129160/selection/8677255573c89f51bbda2655bf0990b3a6ef52dd073a8086551da4668a68282d" "q-129160/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-129160/selection/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" "q-129160/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-129160/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129160" :question/id #uuid "c0420c43-0461-5581-83e8-7d64023b111c" :question/math-academy-id "q-129160" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,1,5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x+4y+4z=18.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+4z & =18 \\\\ -2(-1)+4(2)+4z & =18 \\\\ 4z & =8 \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,2,2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,2,2⟩-⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,4,4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 4+(-3)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+4-12|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129160/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129160"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80122/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "73b546f4-9d39-5203-84f7-1b84335ab0ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80122/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "e365f0d3-9d72-58b2-912e-c233511545d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80122/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer/id #uuid "345f80ac-c931-5a83-90b5-fb4aa98d5940" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80122/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "813489ed-394d-513d-b658-74bb45b077ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80122/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "378690be-b8eb-5cf0-963a-560574f863f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80122/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dab0bcea-5e95-52a9-bc23-94e8b8307c0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80122/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-80122/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-80122/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-80122/selection/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" "q-80122/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-80122/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80122" :question/id #uuid "bb276845-f5c1-5ccd-8c48-c7a56802973e" :question/math-academy-id "q-80122" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,11,10)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x-4y+4z=16.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=2$ and $y=3$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-4y+4z & =16 \\\\ -2(2)-4(3)+4z & =16 \\\\ 4z & =32 \\\\ z & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(2,3,8)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,3,8⟩-⟨-1,11,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-8,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,-4,4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot (-2)+(-8)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 4|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+32-8|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,18\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80122/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80122"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80120/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" :answer/id #uuid "525179ce-af1b-5059-afe0-d8988bf022a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80120/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "30bd6b1a-9ec8-547c-a0bd-1c2d75904207" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80120/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "3cd82b0c-f67b-5c9b-97e5-dc10827317e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80120/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "4072b137-9bf0-5d00-bf59-13d5928380ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80120/selection/d7a2eed6f1a0ddde34dda83c2eff63b490d1c46926c189e70f393bd730e4d502" :answer/id #uuid "e6712e33-a4e3-5dc9-8cdb-13fd64506a75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80120/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b90191e-bc44-501e-ae5d-2f93e1dc7c84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80120/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-80120/selection/219347bb4a6f51134d7f5aff5da33544f44afee934064621ebff9cf9e335ee59" "q-80120/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-80120/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-80120/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-80120/selection/d7a2eed6f1a0ddde34dda83c2eff63b490d1c46926c189e70f393bd730e4d502"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80120" :question/id #uuid "83db8def-7258-521a-a99b-a21020fcb3c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-80120" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-11,-8,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $14x+8y-8z=-6.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=-2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14x+8y-8z & =-6 \\\\ 14(-1)+8(-2)-8z & =-6 \\\\ -8z & =24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,-2,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,-2,-3⟩-⟨-11,-8,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,6,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨14,8,-8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|10\\cdot 14+6\\cdot 8+1\\cdot (-8)|}{\\sqrt{(14)^{2}+{8}^{2}+(-8)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|140+48-8|}{\\sqrt{196+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,180\\,|}{\\sqrt{324}} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80120/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80120"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80119/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "cebfb125-9bdb-5b50-9f0d-7a15eff03ace" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80119/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "65d74063-82bc-5c7b-91b6-cfa70df8d64a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80119/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "fbeeea3a-72cf-526d-9289-a040ebfc4eee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80119/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "257da26b-e999-5075-9b66-5bb25f993a17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80119/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "875f8260-c864-5bb8-b1aa-27e617b1ed0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80119/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd20e745-3e6d-5e19-bfb0-0e9552f20277" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80119/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-80119/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" "q-80119/selection/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" "q-80119/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-80119/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" "q-80119/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80119" :question/id #uuid "e6c9f41a-d083-53d9-b629-704047350f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-80119" :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(6,6,2)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-7y-4z=-26.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-7y-4z & =-26 \\\\ 4(1)-7(2)-4z & =-26 \\\\ -4z & =-16 \\\\ z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,2,4)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,2,4⟩-⟨6,6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-7,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-5)\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-7)+2\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-20+28-8|}{\\sqrt{16+49+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,0\\,|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $P$ lies on the plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80119/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "489887a0-7013-5fb2-8f16-d18616196b0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80119"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4949"] :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,2,-2)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/assets/40ec5f2b2615eedf6b16420a2089b7c377141db46237de35218c5e685b629918.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060274/assets/0589ebbdb2c14b93e1296b9e1f8b0caa0c3df49bff4c9fbb97e4c18102844ec1.png)\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+24-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,6\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4950"] :question/problem "Given that $Q(1,-2,-1)$ lies on the plane $\\Pi:\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle = 4,$ find the shortest distance from $P(0 , -1 , 2)$ to $\\Pi.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-2,-1⟩-⟨0,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 0, -2 \\rangle.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+0+6|}{\\sqrt{4+0+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,8\\,|}{\\sqrt{8}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4951"] :question/problem "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(3 , -10 , 3)$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equation $2x+y-2z = -1$." :question/worked-solution "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=4$ and $y=-5$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2z & =-1 \\\\ 2(4)+(-5)+1 & =2z \\\\ 4 & =2z \\\\ z & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(4, -5, 2)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overrightarrow{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨4,-5,2⟩-⟨3,-10,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle a,b,c \\rangle.$ So, for the plane $\\Pi,$ we have $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 2, 1, -2 \\rangle.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2+5+2|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,9\\,|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
